# Technical Report: Hardened Software Distribution Architecture
## Implementing Zero-Trust OIDC Code Pipelines with Pre-Flight Substrate Audit Guardrails

## 1. Executive Summary
Traditional automated deployment architectures rely heavily on static, long-lived API tokens or authentication passwords stored within repository environment secrets. This dependency creates severe security vectors, including risk of token exfiltration, lack of cryptographic tracking, and vulnerability to downstream supply-chain injection attacks. 

This paper presents a hardened, high-integrity deployment blueprint that eliminates static secrets entirely. By bridging **GitHub Actions OIDC Trusted Publishing** with strict **GitHub Deployment Environments** and a proactive **Substrate Entropy Auditor & Remediator**, we establish an isolated, zero-trust distribution pipeline for Python package deployment to the Python Package Index (PyPI).

