3. Core Implementation Suite


3.1 The GUA-W Pre-Flight Interceptor & Auto-Remediator

The automated dependency remediation routine is encapsulated within the GUAWPreflightAuditor Python utility. This local gatekeeper intercepts build pipelines prior to package compilation, evaluates requirements.txt for unpinned packages (measuring substrate entropy), queries the runner environment via pip freeze to identify exact installed versions, and automatically locks floating versions to strict freeze states. It also performs a structural cryptographic audit to flag unauthorized artifacts before issuing an invariant system status.
The full implementation code for GUAWPreflightAuditor and its corresponding GitHub Actions workflow (python-publish.yml) can be inspected directly in the deployment repository architecture.

3.2 GitHub Actions Configuration

The CI/CD pipeline executes the GUA-W Security Gatekeeper & Auto-Remediator immediately following base dependency installation and prior to distribution building. If drift or floating parameters are discovered, they are resolved locally in the workspace before package compilation and OIDC-authenticated upload to PyPI.

4. Multi-Platform Setup Blueprint


4.1 Securing GitHub Environments

1. Access repository Settings -> Environments on GitHub.
2. Instantiate a protection domain titled pypi.
3. Toggle Required Reviewers and select targeted administrators or team handles.
4. Toggle Prevent self-review to enforce authorization gating.

4.2 Mapping the PyPI OpenID Connect Handshake

1. Authenticate with PyPI, navigate to Account Settings, and click Publishing.
2. Select Create a new pending publisher -> GitHub Actions.
3. Configure registration variables matching your specific organization, repository path, workflow file (python-publish.yml), and environment name (pypi).
